The copy constructor's cost is dominated by the vector copies, and those can't be restructured without changing the class. This version skips the `devFields` copy when the source is empty, which is common, and leaves the copied values and their order unchanged. Expect only a small gain.

```cpp
Mesg::Mesg(const Mesg &mesg)
    : profile(mesg.profile)
    , localNum(mesg.localNum)
    , fields()
    , devFields()
{
    if (!mesg.fields.empty())
        fields.assign(mesg.fields.begin(), mesg.fields.end());
    if (!mesg.devFields.empty())
        devFields.assign(mesg.devFields.begin(), mesg.devFields.end());
}
```